# Event data lives locally and NEVER in git.
# Four people across a 24-hour race is many GB of video, and git history
# retains every byte forever even after a delete.
/data/
*.gpx
*.tcx
manifest.json
*.manifest.json
notes*.csv
people.csv

# The rest of the CSV set, added 2026-07-31 alongside their codecs. These were
# NOT ignored for the first five commits of that work, so a `markers.csv`
# dropped in the repo root would have been committed to a PUBLIC repo — the
# same mistake `notes*.csv` and `people.csv` above exist to prevent.
event.csv
markers.csv
placements.csv

# Worse than the others: the settings file names the URLs of all five data
# files, and a link-shared Google Sheets URL IS a bearer capability — whoever
# holds it reads every note, every name and every timestamp. One leaked
# settings file leaks the whole event.
settings.csv
*-settings.csv

# What the Save button downloads: one zip of notes.csv + people.csv +
# manifest.json, named `meanwhile-<event>-<when>.zip`. See filenameForSave()
# in src/viewer/App.tsx. The bare `meanwhile.zip` is no longer produced —
# kept because saves made before the timestamp was added still carry it.
meanwhile.zip
meanwhile-*.zip

# Media, in case anything lands outside data/. This list is every extension
# ingest accepts — PHOTO_EXTENSIONS and VIDEO_EXTENSIONS in
# src/core/metadata.ts. If that set grows, grow this one with it.
#
# gitignore matching is case-sensitive, so each is listed twice: phones write
# lowercase, cameras write upper. A mixed-case name (.Jpg) would slip through
# these, which is one more reason event media belongs in /data/ rather than
# relying on this net.
#
# `.MTS` COLLIDES WITH TYPESCRIPT — see the negations after the list. AVCHD
# camcorders write `.MTS`, but `.mts` is also TypeScript's ESM module
# extension, and macOS checkouts are case-insensitive, so the uppercase
# pattern silently swallows lowercase source files too. Found the hard way:
# a `.d.mts` written in `scripts/` simply never appeared in `git status`.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.jpe
*.heic
*.heif
*.png
*.webp
*.avif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.gif
*.dng
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm
*.3gp
*.mts
*.JPG
*.JPEG
*.JPE
*.HEIC
*.HEIF
*.PNG
*.WEBP
*.AVIF
*.TIF
*.TIFF
*.GIF
*.DNG
*.MP4
*.MOV
*.M4V
*.AVI
*.MKV
*.WEBM
*.3GP
*.MTS

# Rescue TypeScript module files from the `.MTS` rule above, in the four
# places source actually lives. A path negation rather than a tweak to the
# extension patterns because it has to hold under BOTH a case-sensitive
# checkout (where `*.MTS` misses `.mts`) and a case-insensitive one (where it
# catches it), and only the path differs reliably between a source file and a
# camcorder clip.
#
# The cost, accepted knowingly: a stray `.MTS` clip sitting in one of these
# four locations — including the repo root, which `vite.config.mts` and
# friends need — is no longer caught by this net. Event media belongs in
# `/data/`, which is ignored wholesale above and is unaffected by any of
# this; the extension list only ever existed to catch what lands outside it.
!/src/**/*.mts
!/scripts/**/*.mts
!/tests/**/*.mts
!/*.mts

# Currently inert: tests/fixtures/isobmff.ts and jpeg.ts build hand-crafted
# byte-level parser inputs PROGRAMMATICALLY, in .ts, so nothing above ever
# matches anything under this path today — `git check-ignore -v` confirms
# no file here is ignored, negation or not. Kept as a forward-looking guard
# in case a fixture ever ships as an actual media-extension file (a real
# .jpg or .mp4, capped small) rather than code that builds one; the
# rationale for the fixtures themselves lives in their own header comments,
# there is no separate README here.
!/tests/fixtures/**

# One person's working notes about WHICH event this copy is pointed at — the
# data repo's URL, the photo folder, clock offsets worked out by hand. It is
# per-person and per-event, so it never ships with the app. EVENT.example.md
# is the committed template, meant to be linked from README.md and CLAUDE.md
# so a newcomer finds it — check those files directly for whether that link
# exists yet rather than trusting this comment.
EVENT.md

# Build + tooling
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# Agent worktrees and local Claude Code state. `.claude/worktrees/` holds real
# git checkouts, so `git add -A` will otherwise commit them as embedded repos.
.claude/
